From e39e44bfb70cecfbe97c968bb8cd5b882a1f92c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiasClear <noreply@biasclear.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:54:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Explain: descriptive-vocabulary check for answers; harden the
 model's copy

Red-team findings H1, H2, M1, M2 and L1-L3 (Drive 298), on reviewed head 2299fe1.

- Check 9d (src/howguard.ts). Outside exact quotations of the sentence, every
  word of "how" must come from a reviewed set of words for describing wording,
  from the sentence, or from the move's own name and short line. This runs
  after NFKC, lowercasing and contraction expansion. The check also rejects:
  - verdict, judgement, motive and order words, and verdict phrases;
  - hidden or combining characters, and non-ASCII letters outside quotations;
  - digits the sentence lacks;
  - link, address and phone shapes;
  - an opening imperative;
  - a clause that names the sentence's subject without pointing at the wording;
  - a quotation away from the mark longer than 4 words;
  - other moves' names.
- Check 9c is narrowed to clauses holding a quotation. A quotation other than
  the mark must be described as wording, and no clause may adopt a quotation
  ("points out", "notes", "shows", "explains", "reminds" added). Requiring a
  pointer word in every clause refused most honest answers; 9d now keeps
  unquoted clauses descriptive.
- Side words, the same on both sides: "the far/hard/radical left/right",
  "center-left/right", "lefty/lefties/righty/righties", "dems"/"gop", "libs",
  "illegals".
- prompt.ts asData: the copy the model reads drops format characters, takes
  NFKC, collapses line breaks and maps every angle-bracket look-alike. The
  sentence, its spans and the engine re-check are unchanged.
- Tests:
  - 173 recorded red-team bypasses must stay refused;
  - honest-answer floors from a calibration set: A 80/172 for tuning, and
    B 35/86 held out (the reviewed head scored 37/172 and 17/86);
  - two output tests now expect E_OUT_ECHO for a 5-word quotation of
    injected text.

